{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And he begot sons and daughters.</b> Scripture does not mention 'and he died' for any of these ten generations, as it did for the ten generations from Adam to Noah, because they all died before the subject of the narrative then intended had arrived — namely, the Flood. But these were all alive when the subject of the narrative intended here began — namely, the striving of Abraham our father, more than all the righteous of the preceding generations, to call in the name of YHWH, to make known to humankind His mighty deeds and the glorious majesty of His kingdom, and to draw them with the cords of loving-kindness to serve Him with one accord."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:29:48.931424541Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}